        <body>
            <div xml:id="d482">

                <pb facs="1051" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg955"/>

                <head>No. 450.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 22, 1879</date>.
                        (Received September 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 196.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 146, I have
                    now the honor to inclose herewith a copy and translation of a note from the
                    minister of state, informing me that the excess of tonnage dues exacted at
                    Manila from the American vessels Bullion, Frank Lambeth, Washington, Henry A.
                    Litchfield, and Stephen, has been ordered to be returned to the consignees of
                    said vessels.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d482-a1.xml" xpointer="d482-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
